    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> observations such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></msub><mo>·</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1100</mn></math>. Then the standard deviation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></math> is equal to :"
